--- !u!114 &-1698418311231669840
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 456c7c2b477e4253b9e4faf9ed4b18a9, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.InstructionsParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Title:
    m_Untranslated: Instructions
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: '1. In the <b>Hierarchy</b>, search for and select the part named
      <b>glider_support_02-2</b>.


      2. Right click on the part in the <b>Scene
      view</b> and select <b>Isolate</b>.


      3. Press <b>F</b> to focus the
      object.


      4. Select the <b>Remove Holes</b> option on the <b>ATT toolbar</b>.


      5.
      Set the <b>Max Diameter </b>to <b>0.01</b>.


      6. Select <b>Run</b>. Notice
      that the holes are now removed. This is a simple way to create more optimised
      geometry since there will be less unnecessary vertices in the model now.


      7.
      Repeat the process for the other part named <b>glider_support_02-2</b>.'
  m_CriteriaCompletion: 0
  m_Criteria:
    m_Items: []
--- !u!114 &-1604469990639674176
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 456c7c2b477e4253b9e4faf9ed4b18a9, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.InstructionsParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Title:
    m_Untranslated: Instructions
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "1. To visualize geometry density, select the Debug dropdown
      menu on the <b>Scene view toolbar</b>  and select <b>Vertex Ratio</b>.\n\n2.
      Select <b>Vertex Ratio</b> to highlight mesh density across the model.\n\n3.
      Locate and select one of the red-highlighted parts in the <b>Scene view</b>.
      Check in the <b>Hierarchy</b> to make sure only that part is selected.\n \n4.
      In the <b>ATT</b> toolbar, select <b>Decimate</b>.\n\n5. Set <b>Criterion</b>
      to <b>Target</b>.\n\n6. Set <b>Strategy</b> to <b>Ratio</b>.\n\n7. Adjust the
      <b>Ratio</b> slider to <b>30</b>.\n\n8. Select <b>Run</b>.\n\n9. Repeat this
      for any other parts you want to decimate.\n\n10. Deactivate the debug menu
      when you are done."
  m_CriteriaCompletion: 0
  m_Criteria:
    m_Items: []
